    {
      "filename": "Lascar National Centre for the Performing Arts (The Egg) (4474852849).jpg",
      "title": "File:Lascar National Centre for the Performing Arts (The Egg) (4474852849).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9c/Lascar_National_Centre_for_the_Performing_Arts_%28The_Egg%29_%284474852849%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lascar_National_Centre_for_the_Performing_Arts_(The_Egg)_(4474852849).jpg",
      "width": 3216,
      "height": 2136,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Jorge Láscar from Australia",
      "description": "The National Centre for the Performing Arts and colloquially known as The Egg, is an opera house in Beijing, People's Republic of China. The Centre, an ellipsoid dome of titanium and glass surrounded by an artificial lake, seats 5,452 people in three halls and is almost 12,000 m² in size. It was designed by French architect Paul Andreu. Construction started in December 2001 and the inaugural concert was held in December 2007. The exterior of the theater is a titanium accented glass dome that is completely surrounded by a man-made lake. It is said to look like an egg floating on water. It was designed as an iconic feature, something that would be immediately recognizable, like the Sydney Opera House. The dome measures 212 meters in east-west direction, 144 meters in north-south direction, and is 46 meters high. The main entrance is at the north side. Guests arrive in the building after walking through a hallway that goes underneath the lake. The titanium shell is broken by a glass curtain in north-south direction that gradually widens from top to bottom. [Wikipedia.org]",
      "dateCreated": "2008-11-25 06:20",
      "categories": [
